        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The <strong>absolute value</strong> of a number is its <em>distance from zero</em> when viewed on a number line. </p>",
            "readable_text": "The absolute value of a number is its distance from zero when viewed on a number line.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Distances are never negative. Therefore, the absolute value of a number is always positive or zero.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Distances are never negative. Therefore, the absolute value of a number is always positive or zero.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let&#x27;s consider the number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -5]</span> and its position on a number line, shown below.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Let's consider the number [MATH: -5] and its position on a number line, shown below.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "graphic",
            "normalized_html": "<p><img src=\"/graphics/cf920d91f72b1615210264e172d01bc3\"></p>",
            "readable_text": "[IMG: /graphics/cf920d91f72b1615210264e172d01bc3]",
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "/graphics/cf920d91f72b1615210264e172d01bc3",
                "alt": ""
              }
            ],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The <strong>distance</strong> between <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -5]</span> and zero equals <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5]</span> because <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -5]</span> is five steps away from zero. </p>",
            "readable_text": "The distance between [MATH: -5] and zero equals [MATH: 5] because [MATH: -5] is five steps away from zero.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "graphic",
            "normalized_html": "<p><img src=\"/graphics/18e8471cb3232c92db80fd4281fcc721\"></p>",
            "readable_text": "[IMG: /graphics/18e8471cb3232c92db80fd4281fcc721]",
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "/graphics/18e8471cb3232c92db80fd4281fcc721",
                "alt": ""
              }
            ],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, <em>the absolute value of </em> <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -5]</span> <em>equals</em> <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5.]</span> We write this as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, the absolute value of [MATH: -5] equals [MATH: 5.] We write this as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: | \\, {-5}  \\, |  = 5]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: | \\, {-5} \\, | = 5]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [
          {
            "src": "/graphics/cf920d91f72b1615210264e172d01bc3",
            "alt": ""
