        "title": "A Fast Way of Finding the Absolute Value",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>There is a fast way to find the absolute value of a number:</p>",
            "readable_text": "There is a fast way to find the absolute value of a number:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<ul><li><p>The absolute value of a positive number is equal to itself. For example, \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: |8| = 8 .]</span></p></li><li><p>To find the absolute value of a negative number, we drop the negative sign. For instance,\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: | {-8} | = 8.]</span></p></li></ul>",
            "readable_text": "- The absolute value of a positive number is equal to itself. For example,\n[MATH: |8| = 8 .]\n- To find the absolute value of a negative number, we drop the negative sign. For instance,\n[MATH: | {-8} | = 8.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nThere is a fast way to find the absolute value of a number:\n\nContent:\n- The absolute value of a positive number is equal to itself. For example,\n[MATH: |8| = 8 .]\n- To find the absolute value of a negative number, we drop the negative sign. For instance,\n[MATH: | {-8} | = 8.]"
      },
