          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The number is <em>negative</em> because it is to the <em>left</em> of zero.</p><p>The absolute value of the number is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4,]</span> so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4.]</span> </p><p>The negative number at a distance of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span> from zero is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -4,]</span> so the number is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -4.]</span></p><div class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/eb80c5a808a4166ec5dcdabb8d6a63d0\"></div>",
            "readable_text": "The number is negative because it is to the left of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is [MATH: 4,] so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is [MATH: 4.]\n\nThe negative number at a distance of [MATH: 4] from zero is [MATH: -4,] so the number is [MATH: -4.]\n\n[IMG: /graphics/eb80c5a808a4166ec5dcdabb8d6a63d0]",
